// D1673 — `__array_new__` with an f32 fill, the f32 column of D1669's table. Three spellings
// disagreed: an annotated `f32[]` destination ran, an INFERRED one held an i32 cell over the
// f32 backing (invalid wasm), and a generic instance's parameter fill named no kind at all.
//
// `exprF32Array` lacked the `__array_new__` arm its i64/f64/string/ref siblings carry, so the
// binding's own rep was decided by a reader that could not see the list; and
// `arrNewKindOfElemVKind` excluded `f32` by hand, so the instance's substituted annotation —
// the one channel a monomorphized body still has — answered -1.
//
// The PROOF adds a fraction to an element, so a list allocated at the i32 backing traps or
// prints an integer rather than passing.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function anfMk(): f32 { 7.5 }
// @@VALUE@@
__array_new__(2, anfMk())
// @@TYPE@@
f32[]
// @@FALLBACK@@
__array_new__(2, anfMk())
// @@TEST@@
v.length == 2
// @@HIT@@
print(v[1] + 0.25)
// @@MISS@@
print(-1.0)
// @@WANT@@
7.75
// @@VALUE2@@
__array_new__(3, anfMk())
// @@TYPE2@@
f32[]
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v[2] + 0.25)
// @@WANT2@@
7.75
